1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,470
POV: your AI just learned CAD.

2
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:04,120
Type one sentence:

3
00:00:04,290 --> 00:00:06,180
a phone stand, tilted 15 degrees,

4
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:07,410
with a slot for the cable.

5
00:00:07,890 --> 00:00:08,950
It writes the code,

6
00:00:08,970 --> 00:00:10,510
builds a real 3D model,

7
00:00:10,530 --> 00:00:12,070
and checks that it will actually print.

8
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:13,650
Then it slices it,

9
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:15,300
and can send it straight to a Bambu Lab

10
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:15,850
printer.

11
00:00:16,410 --> 00:00:18,250
It's called text-to-cad.

12
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:21,180
Free, open source, 19,000 GitHub stars.

13
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:22,970
It works with Claude Code,

14
00:00:22,990 --> 00:00:25,310
Codex, Cursor, Gemini and Grok.

15
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,140
Step one: ask.

16
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:28,650
Step two: print.
